  "hardware": {
    "family": "NVIDIA DGX Spark / GB10",
    "testedMachine": "One DGX Spark with 128 GB unified memory",
    "notes": [
      "This version pins the SparkLing 0.1.0 image ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkling:a66a1e6464f4 (also :0.1.0; install tree a66a1e6464f4, Atlas dc0035de5), addressed by its digest. Its build ran 8,827 engine tests with 0 failures.",
      "SparkLing 0.1.0 on one GB10, 2026-11-25, Spark weights, default profile (131,072 tokens) and default drafting, nothing else on the GPU (Enntity/SparkLing results/2026-11-25/README.md): single stream 55.2 tok/s (mean of eight greedy prompts, 256 tokens, thinking off), drafted text equal to plain decode on 8 of 8; aggregate 54.6 / 61.1 / 77.3 / 104.0 tok/s at 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 clients, median time to first token 1.03 s at 8; 29 of 30 arithmetic word problems with thinking on; 10 of 10 single-tool calls; a red-to-blue clip, a counting clip as GIF and MP4, a 90 s 720p clip, an invoice and a grid all read correctly.",
      "In the same file, vLLM's MTP x3 serving the same NVFP4A16 checkpoint on the same Spark read 40.2 tok/s single-stream and 44.6 / 59.2 / 68.8 / 109.2 at 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 clients (SparkLing's comparison runs used an 8,192-token window, within 3% of the release image).",
      "Spark drafts one token per step with the checkpoint's own MTP predictor (SPARKLING_DRAFTER=mtp) for one active request and decodes plainly from two (ATLAS_MTP_MAX_SEQS=1); Atlas verifies each draft with serial decode's arithmetic, so greedy text matches drafting off.",
      "The max mode serves Ling's full 262,144-token window. There the BF16 KV pool (28.4 GiB) and the weights do not fit together, so Atlas reads some experts from the model files: one stream decoded 11.4 tok/s at 0.80 GPU memory utilization and 6.2 at 0.88, against 54.9 at 131,072 tokens with the same text.",
      "Profiles (SparkLing install/profiles, all BF16 KV and prefix caching, 2,048-token prefill chunks or 8,192 with NVFP4 prefill, ffmpeg video decoding on): default 8 requests at 0.80 GPU memory utilization, saver 1 request of 8,192 tokens at 0.70, max 16 requests at 0.88. Requests the KV pool cannot hold yet wait rather than fail. Strict shares one KV pool between requests (ATLAS_KV_MAX_BLOCKS in each profile).",
      "Strict serves the original checkpoint for reference. It does not fit in memory, so Atlas pages experts from the checkpoint on disk and it decodes far slower than Spark; Strict was not part of the 0.1.0 release measurement.",
      "Peak host memory was not measured per mode. LLooM reserves an estimate: saver 92 GB, default 104 GB, max 114 GB. The container is capped at 114 GiB because a GB10 that runs out of shared memory hangs instead of killing a process. In the default and max modes little else should use this Spark's GPU memory.",
      "The engine serves 127.0.0.1:8897 (fixed by the image) with host networking, so only one SparkLing model runs at a time; its memory reservation keeps LLooM from starting the other beside it. Text, image and video input: OpenAI image_url parts and video_url parts (animated GIF decoded in-process, MP4 and WebM through the image's ffmpeg).",
      "Licenses: the Atlas engine and SparkLing's install tools run from the image and are AGPL-3.0-only (not included in LLooM). inclusionAI/Ling-3.2-air and primitive-ai/Ling-3.2-air-NVFP4A16 are MIT."
    ]
  },
